Shopkeeper Squabble:
This just occurred to me, and I wondered if anyone has ever tried it.
If anyone has, I'd love to know how well it worked. It sounds like
great fun and I intend to try it at the earliest opportunity:

To play Shopkeeper Squabble you will need:
-A level with multiple shops (minetown or various Slashem levels)
-Teleport control.
-a means of teleporting at will. 
-A ring of conflict
-Telepathy and a blindfold.

How to play:
-Go to each shop in turn, pick up loads of good stuff, teleport to the
next shop.
-When you have all shopkeepers (barring Izchak, if applicable) and
about a zillion Kops out looking for you, put on the blindfold and
teleport to a safe location.
-Use teleportation to keep yourself out of harm's way while steering
the group of shopkeepers and Kops into a single crowd. Maybe you could
shut them all in a big room somewhere.
-When you have a nice, compact, angry mob, put on the ring of conflict
and watch it turn upon itself.
-When only one shopkeep remains, finish him off and mop up all the
cash, wands etc.

**Unsuitable for lawful players due to extensive robbery and wholesale
grisly slaughter of innocents.
**Unsuitable for children under age 4 due to =oC choking hazard.
